      <title>Jim Ratcliffe: Billionaire Tax Exile Is Making One Valid Point About Britain</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-09-23/jim-ratcliffe-man-utd-tax-exile-makes-one-valid-point-about-uk-government</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">ef8d56f54546965f0abac57a</guid>
      <pubDate>Wed, 23 Sep 2026 04:00:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Billionaire Jim Ratcliffe suggests Manchester United Plc is an example of how to run Britain better. And the response from many has been: Who’s he to tell the UK what to do? Ratcliffe is a tax exile with a fortune derived from fossil fuels and some ugly views on immigration. Nor are Man Utd fans a happy bunch. But ignore all that and he has a simple point worth heeding. Whether in business or government, sometimes you have to cut costs.</description>
